---
import { version } from "../../../../npm/magistr/package.json";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Workflow from "../components/Workflow.astro";
import ProductEvidence from "../components/ProductEvidence.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"Magistr","url":"https://magistr.dev"},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Magistr","softwareVersion":version,"description":"The workflow layer for coding agents. Plan the work, review source changes and keep a record of the checks.","url":"https://magistr.dev","applicationCategory":"DeveloperApplication","operatingSystem":"macOS (Apple Silicon)","downloadUrl":"https://magistr.dev/docs/installation","softwareRequirements":"macOS 15 or later; Rust 1.95 or later; repository access"}
];
---
<Base title="Magistr — Plan the work. Prove the change." description="The workflow layer for Codex and Claude Code. Connect roadmaps, source changes and recorded checks, and carry the work into your next session." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero section-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span> The workflow layer for coding agents</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Plan the work.<br /><span>Prove the change.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Give Codex or Claude Code a project workflow that lasts: a roadmap to follow, source changes to review, and checks you can trace.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a id="install-btn" class="button button-primary" href="#install">Try the source preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-quiet" href="#workflow">Explore the workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">Apple Silicon macOS <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> v{version} preview<br />Building from source requires repository access.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="work-schematic" aria-label="Magistr connects a plan, a source change, a check and a saved record">
        <div class="schematic-top"><span class="mono-label">From intent to evidence</span><span aria-hidden="true">M / 01</span></div>
        <ol>
          <li><span class="schematic-number">01</span><div><strong>Plan</strong><span>A goal. A scope. A way to check it.</span></div></li>
          <li><span class="schematic-number">02</span><div><strong>Change</strong><span>Find the source. Make a verified edit.</span></div></li>
          <li><span class="schematic-number">03</span><div><strong>Check</strong><span>Run the tests. Keep the result.</span></div></li>
          <li><span class="schematic-number">04</span><div><strong>Continue</strong><span>The next session starts with the record.</span></div></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="schematic-foot">Your agent. Your project. A shared thread of work.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="connection-strip">
      <div class="section-shell connection-inner">
        <p>Works with the agent<br /><strong>you already use.</strong></p>
        <div class="connection-agents"><span>Codex</span><span>Claude Code</span></div>
        <p class="connection-detail">Connected through MCP.<br />Plans and work history stay in your project.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section id="workflow" class="section-shell section-block" aria-labelledby="workflow-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="section-heading heading-split">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">01 / The workflow</p><h2 id="workflow-title">One task.<br />A complete line of evidence.</h2></div>
        <p>A small bug makes the process easy to see. Follow a real Contact list task from a failing test to a saved result, then see a fresh agent session read it back.</p>
      </div>
      <Workflow />
    </section>

    <section id="product" class="product-section" aria-labelledby="product-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="section-shell section-block">
        <div class="product-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / What Magistr adds</p>
          <h2 id="product-title">Keep the reasoning.<br />Inspect the work.<br /><span>Know what passed.</span></h2>
          <p>Your agent brings the coding ability. Magistr connects it to a durable plan, source tools and a work history you can return to.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/concepts">How the pieces fit <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="product-details">
          <article><span class="mono-label">Direction</span><h3>A roadmap with a next step.</h3><p>Set goals, dependencies and acceptance checks. Ask your agent to work on one ready item, or resume the item already in progress.</p><code>magistr next</code></article>
          <article><span class="mono-label">Execution</span><h3>Changes you can inspect.</h3><p>Magistr’s source tools search and read your code, check edits against the current file, and keep a change journal. Save the decisions that explain the change.</p></article>
          <article><span class="mono-label">Verification</span><h3>“Done” comes with a record.</h3><p>Run your project’s checks and retain the command, exit code and source identity. Required checks govern roadmap completion. A passing check tells you exactly what was tested.</p></article>
          <article><span class="mono-label">Continuity</span><h3>Context beyond the conversation.</h3><p>Plans, findings, actions and results remain available to the next session. Your agent can read the record, inspect the current code and continue the work.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="evidence" class="section-shell section-block evidence-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="section-heading heading-split">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Inside the tools</p><h2 id="evidence-title">Read the actual record.</h2></div>
        <p>Real Codex and Claude Code sessions, plus the Magistr desktop preview. Open any original to inspect the details.</p>
      </div>
      <ProductEvidence />
    </section>

    <section id="install" class="install-section" aria-labelledby="install-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="section-shell section-block">
        <div class="install-grid">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">04 / Start with your project</p>
            <h2 id="install-title">Give the next task<br />a better starting point.</h2>
            <p>Magistr v{version} is a source preview for Apple Silicon macOS. Registry packages are not published yet. Building it requires repository access.</p>
            <p class="install-requirements">macOS 15+ <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Rust 1.95+ <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Your own agent account</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/docs/installation">Read the installation guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="code-panel">
            <div class="code-label"><span>Install from source</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy="source-install" hidden>Copy commands</button></div>
            <pre id="source-install"><code>git clone https://github.com/AlrikOlson/magistr.git
cd magistr
cargo install --locked --path crates/magistr-cli
magistr --version</code></pre>
            <p class="copy-status" data-copy-status role="status"></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="setup-steps">
          <li><span class="step-number">01</span><div><h3>Connect your agent</h3><p><code>magistr init .</code> sets up your project and the agents you choose.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="step-number">02</span><div><h3>Check the setup</h3><p><code>magistr doctor .</code> checks the connection and explains anything that needs attention.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="step-number">03</span><div><h3>Choose the first task</h3><p>Ask for a plan. Use <code>$next</code> in Codex or <code>/next</code> in Claude Code when you’re ready. Setup does not start implementation.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-shell docs-index" aria-label="Further reading">
      <p>Go a little deeper.</p>
      <div class="doc-links">
        <a href="/docs/concepts"><strong>How Magistr works</strong><span>Planning, source changes, checks and saved work.</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/docs/installation"><strong>Set up your project</strong><span>Installation, agent connections and troubleshooting.</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<script>
  const copy = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]");
  if (copy) {
    copy.hidden = false;
    copy.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const text = document.getElementById(copy.dataset.copy!)?.textContent ?? "";
      const status = document.querySelector("[data-copy-status]")!;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        status.textContent = "Commands copied.";
      } catch {
        status.textContent = "Copy is unavailable. Select the commands above to copy them.";
      }
    });
  }
</script>
